his face  he told me i'd been screaming in my  sleep and asked me if i'd been having  that dream again it made me feel like an  idiot but i had to nod and tell him yes  it was the same one this weird nightmare  i've been having day after day and  despite it almost always being the same  thing it somehow never got any less  frightening there was no way to even  describe the profound sense of dread i  felt walking down those stairs and  finally seeing what was waiting for me  below even though i could never actually  remember what it was upon waking steve  told me not to worry about it and toss  some clothes onto my bed he assured me  that it was probably just final stress  seeing as we were a mere few months from  graduating i needed to be up in adam  today we were touring one of our first  choice colleges my brother and i had  always been close even if we hadn't been  fraternal twins i think we still would  have been best friends all through  elementary middle and high school we  were practically joined at the hip so it  only made sense that when we were  getting close to graduation we wanted to  go to the same college we'd be friends  to the end till we were old men on the  porch and rocking chairs it so happened  that we were together in the end just  not in the way i'd hoped the two of us  arrived to check out the potential  college a few hours later it was a nice  day out the brightness of the sky and  the lush greenery across campus quickly  banished the bitter memories of that bad  dream high school hadn't exactly been a  picnic for me i'm the nervous type if  you couldn't already tell steve who was  the more outgoing and confident one  always looked out for me he'd always  been there whenever i was dealing with  bullies or academic stress but at  college i felt like i could reinvent  myself and become the kind of person i'd  always wanted to be as we hop from  building to building across the tour  checking out the different facilities  and attending a few sample lectures and  seminars i was only becoming more  confident that college would be the  place for me to finally bloom it was  perfect for me but despite this college  being exactly what i'd wanted in terms  of lifestyle and academic pursuits there  was a certain stain on its reputation if  any university is around long enough for  any building at all for that matter  weird incidents are bound to accumulate  some places have ghost or cryptid  sightings this college had  disappearances not just one or two six  different students and one janitor had  disappeared from the campus the people  had nothing in common except for the  fact that they frequented the college  ages races genders and majors varied  across all the missing people and none  of them had known each other no notes  were given no clues discovered no  remains ever found a number of the cases  are even still open today it's a  frightening thought that people can just  drop off the face of the earth like that  and never be found there are over half a  million missing person cases in the  united states back in 2020 alone it's  more common than you think still i  comforted myself with the knowledge that  thousands of new students came in and  out of the college every year and only a  handful of disappearances what were the  chances that something bad would ever  happen to me though to be fair every  person who actually did disappear in  their last moments thought what are the  chances something like this would happen  to me too we were several hours into the  tour when the coffee steve had on the  way over finally caught up with him he  needed to go bad so we asked our tour  guide whether there was a bathroom  anywhere around here she told him that  he could find one pretty easily on the  ground floor of any administrative  building nearby in the meantime we'd be  making our way over to lecture hall 2b  so he could simply catch up with us  there once he was done steve left and i  didn't think anything of it 