oor stay away it keeps going  something down here don't come looking  oh god if i was scared before i was  utterly mortified now i couldn't just  leave my brother in a situation like  this no matter what he told me to do i  had to find him somehow i just had to  nobody else seemed to take it seriously  but i somehow knew he was in the most  terrible danger that's when i decided to  head to the one place i believed he  would be the administrative building it  was such an unremarkable little building  hardly the kind of place where you'd  expect some terrible secret to be hiding  but dangerous things often hide in plain  sight things like the door it was one of  those things from steve's message that  had stuck in my head the door call it  instinct call it intuition call it blind  dumb luck but when i was standing in  front of an average looking door in that  unremarkable administrative building i  knew i was staring at the exact door  that my brother had been talking about  it radiated bad vibes dark energy was  practically humming off of it but i  wouldn't let that stop me perhaps i was  stupid going in without help while it's  easy to criticize from the safety of  your home it's worth remembering we do  silly things when we're afraid and i  mean this was my brother were talking  about here no one in the world was more  important to me than him no one the  second i entered the room beyond the  door something changed it was like  stepping into another world entirely the  air was thick and oppressive the floor  below me and the walls around me were  ungodly cold but most remarkable of all  was the dark even my phone's flashlight  at full power barely made a dent i don't  think i'd ever seen anything so truly  impenetrably dark outside of a certain  nightmare anyway that was when i finally  realized where i was standing at the top  of the stairs those  stairs the stairs that had been haunting  my restless sleep a single winding  stairwell down into the void every part  of me wanted to run and scream and hide  but i couldn't i knew that if it were me  trapped down there steve wouldn't have  hesitated he would have charged down  there and helped me now i had to do the  same for him after all we all know that  in real life there's no such thing as  monsters and how deep could a staircase  really go anyway that question was soon  put to the test as i descended down into  the pit i counted 13 steps each time  before reaching a small platform there  were strange markings and scratches on  the wall the further i descended every  footstep i took echoed on and on and on  i must have been walking for a solid 15  minutes traveling impossibly deep when i  finally heard something else i called  out steve's name but quickly realized it  wasn't him it was a little girl weeping  a few hundred feet below i couldn't tell  if she was afraid and pain or both but  hearing it put ice in my veins what the  hell was going on down there had whoever  taken her taken steve too what exactly  was i dealing with these were the  questions racing through my mind as i  got deeper and deeper into the belly of  the beast time ceased to matter as the  flights went on and on beneath me even  descending into deeper colder darkness i  was literally walking into my own  nightmare but seeing as the only  alternative was leaving my brother to  die down here i couldn't do anything  else i was down countless flights of  stairs when i finally saw him he was a  distant pale speck dithering and afraid  he was a full flight down for me i was  so happy to see him that at first i  didn't even notice anything was wrong as  i got closer i began to realize that  this wasn't the steve i knew the dread  crept into me spreading through every  cell like a virus i finally knew why i  recognized it it was the thing for my  dreams the monster whose appearance  always brought those terrible nightmares  to an end but what did it mean to see it  in real life it was steve's face but it  seemed larger and deathly pale i froze  and as the face drew closer to me i  realized it had no irises no pupils no  nostrils and no mouth it wasn't my  brother it looked like a terrible  death-like mask modeled after him i  tried to scream as it appeared right in  front of me just as i had in my dreams  but it was too late long gnarled fingers  curled around my torso and crushed my  ribs it was a pain more intense than i  thought possible and soon even my vision  went black as i was dragged down to the  darkness below the last thought on my  mind was stee i'm so sorry i couldn't  save you i couldn't even save myself  now go check out  scp-087 the stairwell and the secret at  the bottom of scp-087 explained for more  takes on the terrifying secret of the  stairwell

